6","T9"],"criteria":["E6","E1"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC2: 'If current-history position resolution fails, the verifier retains the recorded ledger commit SHA as its fallback'","Plan bullet 1 describes only a regression that 'proves the current verifier misclassifies the authentic ledger entry' — a success/detect case","The described 'existing null-commit recovery behavior' is a different path (null SHA), not the new non-null unresolvable-position fallback"],"finding":"AC #2 ('If current-history position resolution fails, the verifier retains the recorded ledger commit SHA as its fallback') is marked code-verifiable, but the described regression only proves the success case (authentic entry re-resolved after rewrite). No step describes a fixture that forces position resolution to FAIL for a non-null-SHA entry, so the fail-closed fallback path is claimed but not exercised.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4912f964432bfef9","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria line 2; Plan bullet 1 (regression) and bullet 2","norm_id":"n92f00b3364dcfdd4","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["A ledger entry whose position no longer resolves in the current history (e.g. its position row was pruned) must fall back to the recorded SHA — untested, could regress silently"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add a test fixture whose ledger position cannot be resolved against the rewritten history and assert the verifier uses the stored commit_sha as the fail-closed fallback.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_